# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"
msgstr "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) is a variant of VQE that allows "
"obtaining the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with "
"eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq"
" k$. Without loss of generality, we assume that "
"$\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE introduces a new idea by "
"adding weights to help prioritize optimizing for the term with the largest "
"weight.\n"
msgstr ""
"[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) es una variante de VQE que permite"
" obtener los primeros $k$ valores propios de un observable $\\hat{H}$ con "
"valores propios $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, donde "
"$N\\geq k$. Sin pérdida de generalidad, suponemos que "
"$\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE introduce una nueva idea "
"al añadir pesos para priorizar la optimización del término con mayor peso.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of "
"variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Un diagrama que muestra cómo el VQE de búsqueda en subespacios utiliza los"
" componentes del algoritmo "
"variacional.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement this algorithm, we need $k$ mutually orthogonal reference "
"states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, meaning $\\langle \\rho_j | "
"\\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$. These states can be "
"constructed using Pauli operators. The cost function of this algorithm is "
"then:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para implementar este algoritmo, necesitamos $k$ estados de referencia "
"mutuamente ortogonales $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, lo que "
"significa que $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ para "
"$j,l<k$. Estos estados pueden construirse usando operadores de Pauli. La "
"función de coste de este algoritmo es:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | "
"U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | "
"U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $w_j$ is an arbitrary positive number such that if $j<l<k$ then "
"$w_j>w_l$, and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ is the user-defined variational form.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $w_j$ es un número positivo arbitrario tal que si $j<l<k$ entonces "
"$w_j>w_l$, y $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ es la forma variacional definida por el "
"usuario.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The SSVQE algorithm relies on the fact that eigenstates corresponding to "
"different eigenvalues are mutually orthogonal. Specifically, the inner "
"product of $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ and "
"$U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ can be expressed as:\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo SSVQE se basa en el hecho de que los estados propios "
"correspondientes a distintos valores propios son mutuamente ortogonales. En "
"particular, el producto interno de $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ y "
"$U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ puede expresarse como:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"
msgstr "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first equality holds because $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ is a quantum "
"operator and is therefore unitary. The last equality holds because of the "
"orthogonality of the reference states $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. The fact that "
"orthogonality is preserved through unitary transformations is deeply related"
" to the principle of conservation of information, as expressed in quantum "
"information science. Under this view, non-unitary transformations represent "
"processes where information is either lost or injected.\n"
msgstr ""
"La primera igualdad es válida porque $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ es un operador "
"cuántico y, por tanto, unitario. La última igualdad se cumple por la "
"ortogonalidad de los estados de referencia $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. El hecho de "
"que la ortogonalidad se conserve a través de transformaciones unitarias está"
" profundamente relacionado con el principio de conservación de la "
"información, tal como se expresa en la ciencia de la información cuántica. "
"Desde esta perspectiva, las transformaciones no unitarias representan "
"procesos en los que se pierde o se inyecta información.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Weights $w_j$ help ensure that all the states are eigenstates. If the "
"weights are sufficiently different, the term with the largest weight (that "
"is, $w_0$) will be given priority during optimization over the others. As a "
"result, the resulting state $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ will "
"become the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$. Because $\\{ "
"U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ are mutually "
"orthogonal, the remaining states will be orthogonal to it and, therefore, "
"contained in the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues "
"$\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Los pesos $w_j$ ayudan a garantizar que todos los estados sean estados "
"propios. Si los pesos son suficientemente distintos, el término con mayor "
"peso (es decir, $w_0$) recibirá prioridad durante la optimización sobre los "
"demás. Como resultado, el estado resultante $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 "
"\\rangle$ se convertirá en el estado propio correspondiente a $\\lambda_0$. "
"Dado que $\\{ U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ son "
"mutuamente ortogonales, los estados restantes serán ortogonales a este y, "
"por tanto, estarán contenidos en el subespacio correspondiente a los valores"
" propios $\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying the same argument to the rest of the terms, the next priority would"
" then be the term with weight $w_1$, so $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 "
"\\rangle$ would be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_1$, and the "
"other terms would be contained in the eigenspace of "
"$\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicando el mismo argumento al resto de los términos, la siguiente "
"prioridad sería el término con peso $w_1$, de modo que "
"$U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ sería el estado propio "
"correspondiente a $\\lambda_1$, y los demás términos estarían contenidos en "
"el espacio propio de $\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By reasoning inductively, we deduce that $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle$ will be an approximate eigenstate of $\\lambda_j$ for $0\\leq j < "
"k.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Razonando inductivamente, deducimos que $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle$ será un estado propio aproximado de $\\lambda_j$ para $0\\leq j < "
"k.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-1}"
msgstr "Esquema teórico {#theoretical-layout-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SSVQE's can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "El algoritmo SSVQE puede resumirse de la siguiente manera:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare several reference states by applying a unitary U_R to k different "
"computational basis states\n"
msgstr ""
"Preparar varios estados de referencia aplicando un unitario U_R a $k$ "
"estados distintos de la base computacional\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This algorithm requires the usage of $k$ mutually orthogonal reference "
"states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, such that $\\langle \\rho_j |"
" \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Este algoritmo requiere el uso de $k$ estados de referencia mutuamente "
"ortogonales $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, de modo que $\\langle "
"\\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ para $j,l<k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to each reference "
"state, resulting in the following ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicar la forma variacional $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ a cada estado de "
"referencia, obteniendo el siguiente ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if a similar problem is available (usually found via "
"classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr ""
"Arranque en $i=0$ si se dispone de un problema similar (normalmente obtenido"
" mediante simulación clásica o muestreo).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j "
"\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Evaluar la función de coste $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j "
"\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ para todos los estados preparados en un ordenador cuántico.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be separated into calculating the expectation value for an "
"observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ and multiplying that result by $w_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto puede separarse en el cálculo del valor esperado de un observable "
"$\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ y la multiplicación del resultado por $w_j$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Afterward, the cost function returns the sum of all weighted expectation "
"values.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, la función de coste devuelve la suma de todos los valores "
"esperados ponderados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a classical optimizer to determine the next set of parameters "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usar un optimizador clásico para determinar el siguiente conjunto de "
"parámetros $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the above steps until convergence is achieved.\n"
msgstr "Repetir los pasos anteriores hasta alcanzar la convergencia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will be reconstructing SSVQE's cost function in the assessment, but we "
"have the following snippet to motivate your solution:\n"
msgstr ""
"Reconstruirás la función de coste de SSVQE en la evaluación, pero aquí "
"tienes el siguiente fragmento para orientar tu solución:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"
msgstr ""
"Deflación cuántica variacional (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) is an iterative method that extends "
"VQE to obtain the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with "
"eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq"
" k$, instead of only the first. For the rest of this section, we will "
"assume, without loss of generality, that "
"$\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD introduces the "
"notion of a penalty cost to guide the optimization process.\n"
msgstr ""
"[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) es un método iterativo que extiende "
"VQE para obtener los primeros $k$ valores propios de un observable "
"$\\hat{H}$ con valores propios $\\{\\lambda_0, "
"\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, donde $N\\geq k$, en lugar de solo el "
"primero. Para el resto de esta sección, asumiremos, sin pérdida de "
"generalidad, que $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD"
" introduce la noción de un coste de penalización para guiar el proceso de "
"optimización.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduces a penalty term, denoted as $\\beta$, to balance the contribution of each overlap term to the cost. This penalty term serves to penalize the optimization process if orthogonality is not achieved. We impose this constraint because the eigenstates of an observable, or a Hermitian operator, corresponding to different eigenvalues are always mutually orthogonal, or can be made to be so in the case of degeneracy or repeated eigenvalues. Thus, by enforcing orthogonality with the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$, we are effectively optimizing over the subspace that corresponds to the rest of the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Here, $\\lambda_1$ is the lowest eigenvalue from the rest of the eigenvalues and, therefore, the optimal solution of the new problem can be obtained using the variational theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Un diagrama que muestra cómo VQD usa los componentes de un algoritmo variacional.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduce un término de penalización, denotado como $\\beta$, para equilibrar la contribución de cada término de solapamiento al coste. Este término de penalización sirve para sancionar el proceso de optimización si no se logra la ortogonalidad. Imponemos esta restricción porque los estados propios de un observable, o de un operador hermítico, correspondientes a distintos valores propios son siempre mutuamente ortogonales, o pueden hacerse así en el caso de degeneración o valores propios repetidos. Así, al imponer la ortogonalidad con el estado propio correspondiente a $\\lambda_0$, estamos optimizando efectivamente sobre el subespacio que corresponde al resto de los valores propios $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Aquí, $\\lambda_1$ es el valor propio más bajo de entre los restantes y, por tanto, la solución óptima del nuevo problema puede obtenerse usando el teorema variacional.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The general idea behind VQD is to use VQE as usual to obtain the lowest "
"eigenvalue $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv "
"C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ along with the corresponding (approximate) "
"eigenstate $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ for some optimal parameter "
"vector $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Then, to obtain the next eigenvalue $\\lambda_1 >"
" \\lambda_0$, instead of minimizing the cost function $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) "
":= \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, we optimize:\n"
msgstr ""
"La idea general detrás de VQD es usar VQE de la forma habitual para obtener "
"el valor propio más bajo $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv "
"C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ junto con el estado propio (aproximado) "
"correspondiente $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ para algún vector de "
"parámetros óptimo $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Luego, para obtener el siguiente valor"
" propio $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_0$, en lugar de minimizar la función de coste"
" $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, optimizamos:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The positive value $\\beta_0$ should ideally be greater than "
"$\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"El valor positivo $\\beta_0$ debería ser idealmente mayor que "
"$\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This introduces a new cost function that can be viewed as a constrained "
"problem, where we minimize $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ subject to"
" the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to the previously obtained"
" $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$, with $\\beta_0$ acting as a penalty "
"term if the constraint is not satisfied.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto introduce una nueva función de coste que puede verse como un problema "
"con restricciones, donde minimizamos $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = "
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ "
"sujeto a la restricción de que el estado debe ser ortogonal al "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ previamente obtenido, con $\\beta_0$ "
"actuando como término de penalización si la restricción no se satisface.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, this new problem can be interpreted as running VQE on the new"
" observable:\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativamente, este nuevo problema puede interpretarse como ejecutar VQE "
"sobre el observable:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the solution to the new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_1}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"To obtain the third eigenvalue $\\lambda_2$, the cost function to optimize is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Asumiendo que la solución al nuevo problema es $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, el valor esperado de $\\hat{H}$ (no de $\\hat{H_1}$) debería ser $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"Para obtener el tercer valor propio $\\lambda_2$, la función de coste a optimizar es:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\beta_1$ is a positive constant large enough to enforce "
"orthogonality of the solution state to both "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ and $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. "
"This penalizes states in the search space that do not meet this requirement,"
" effectively restricting the search space. Thus, the optimal solution of the"
" new problem should be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $\\beta_1$ es una constante positiva suficientemente grande para "
"imponer la ortogonalidad del estado solución tanto con "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ como con "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. Esto penaliza los estados del espacio de"
" búsqueda que no cumplen este requisito, restringiendo efectivamente dicho "
"espacio. Así, la solución óptima del nuevo problema debería ser el estado "
"propio correspondiente a $\\lambda_2$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like the previous case, this new problem can also be interpreted as VQE with"
" the observable:\n"
msgstr ""
"Al igual que en el caso anterior, este nuevo problema también puede "
"interpretarse como VQE con el observable:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the solution to this new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_2}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Analogously, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue $\\lambda_{k-1}$, you would minimize the cost function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Si la solución a este nuevo problema es $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, el valor esperado de $\\hat{H}$ (no de $\\hat{H_2}$) debería ser $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"De forma análoga, para obtener el $k$-ésimo valor propio $\\lambda_{k-1}$, minimizarías la función de coste:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remember that we defined $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ such that $\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = "
"\\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. This problem is equivalent to minimizing "
"$C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ but with the constraint that the state must "
"be orthogonal to $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, "
"\\cdots, k-1}$, thereby restricting the search space to the subspace "
"corresponding to the eigenvalues "
"$\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que definimos $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ de forma que $\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = "
"\\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. Este problema es equivalente a minimizar "
"$C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ pero con la restricción de que el estado debe"
" ser ortogonal a $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, "
"\\cdots, k-1}$, restringiendo así el espacio de búsqueda al subespacio "
"correspondiente a los valores propios "
"$\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This problem is equivalent to a VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr "Este problema es equivalente a un VQE con el observable:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As you can see from the process, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue, you need "
"the (approximate) eigenstates of the previous $k-1$ eigenvalues, so you "
"would need to run VQE a total of $k$ times. Therefore, VQD's cost function "
"is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Como puedes ver en el proceso, para obtener el $k$-ésimo valor propio "
"necesitas los estados propios (aproximados) de los $k-1$ valores propios "
"anteriores, por lo que tendrías que ejecutar VQE un total de $k$ veces. Por "
"tanto, la función de coste de VQD es la siguiente:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-2}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "VQD's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "El esquema de VQD puede resumirse así:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a reference operator $U_R$\n"
msgstr "Preparar un operador de referencia $U_R$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to the reference state, "
"creating the following ansatze $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicar la forma variacional $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ al estado de "
"referencia, creando los siguientes ansätze $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via "
"classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr ""
"Arrancar en $i=0$ si se dispone de un problema similar (típicamente hallado "
"mediante simulación clásica o muestreo).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluate the cost function $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, which involves computing "
"$k$ excited states and an array of $\\beta$'s defining the overlap penalty "
"for each overlap term.\n"
msgstr ""
"Evaluar la función de coste $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, que implica calcular $k$ "
"estados excitados y un array de $\\beta$'s que define la penalización por "
"solapamiento para cada término.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the expectation value for an observable $\\langle "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ "
"for each $k$\n"
msgstr ""
"Calcular el valor esperado de un observable $\\langle "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ "
"para cada $k$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the penalty $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Calcular la penalización $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The cost function should then return the sum of these two terms\n"
msgstr "La función de coste debe devolver la suma de estos dos términos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a classical optimizer to choose the next set of parameters "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usar un optimizador clásico para elegir el siguiente conjunto de parámetros "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat this process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Repetir este proceso hasta alcanzar la convergencia.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this implementation, we'll create a function for an overlap penalty. "
"This penalty will be used in the cost function at each iteration. This "
"process will be repeated for each excited state\n"
msgstr ""
"Para esta implementación, crearemos una función para una penalización por "
"solapamiento. Esta penalización se usará en la función de coste en cada "
"iteración. Este proceso se repetirá para cada estado excitado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-"
"outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"
